      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The mantle is Earth's thickest layer, occupying nearly 83% of Earth's volume.",
        "It extends vertically from a depth of 35 km down to 2900 km.",
        "The upper mantle comprises both the rigid lithosphere and the asthenosphere.",
        "The asthenosphere lies between 100–350 km depth and is partially molten.",
        "Plate movement is driven by convection currents operating within the mantle."
